\draw[thick] (3.5,2.7)--(4.75,2.7);
\draw[thick] (0.75,2.5)--(0.75,2.9);
\draw[thick] (4.75,2.5)--(4.75,2.9);
\draw[thick,fill=none] (2.25,2.3) rectangle (3.5,3.1);
\draw[thick] (2.5,2.3)--(2.5,3.1);
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.55,2.7) {Quan};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Quan's median ($50$) is lower than Priest's median ($55$), so the commentator's claim about the median is wrong.
Priest: IQR $=65-40=25$.
Quan: IQR $=70-45=25$.
The box widths are equal, so the middle half of their scores is equally consistent. Priest has the higher typical score; these two measures do not support the claim that Quan is clearly better.

